VibeRadiant Build Instructions
====================================

VibeRadiant now uses a native Meson + Ninja build graph.
No legacy Make wrapper is used by Meson anymore.

Quick start (Meson/Ninja)
-------------------------

1) Configure (the all-in-one gamepack is downloaded during the first install):
   meson setup build --prefix "$(pwd)/install" -Dinstall_data=true -Ddownload_gamepacks=allinone

2) Build:
   meson compile -C build

3) Stage runtime tree:
   meson install -C build --no-rebuild --tags runtime

Core Meson options
------------------

- `-Dbuild_profile=release|debug|extradebug|extradebug_quicker|profile|native`
- `-Dinstall_data=true|false`
- `-Dinstall_dlls=true|false` (Windows)
- `-Ddownload_gamepacks=no|yes|all|allinone`
- `-Dgamepack_source=VibePack`
- `-Dassimp_internal=true|false`
- `-Dqt_major=5|6`
- `-Dradiant_aboutmsg="<text>"`

Example profiles
----------------

Release/dev-fast:
  meson setup build-release --prefix "$(pwd)/install" -Dbuild_profile=release -Dinstall_data=false -Dinstall_dlls=false -Ddownload_gamepacks=no
  meson compile -C build-release
  meson install -C build-release --no-rebuild --tags runtime

Debug:
  meson setup build-debug --prefix "$(pwd)/install" -Dbuild_profile=debug -Dinstall_data=false -Dinstall_dlls=false -Ddownload_gamepacks=no
  meson compile -C build-debug
  meson install -C build-debug --no-rebuild --tags runtime

Full packaging-style install:
  meson setup build-full --prefix "$(pwd)/install" -Dbuild_profile=release -Dinstall_data=true -Dinstall_dlls=true -Ddownload_gamepacks=allinone
  meson compile -C build-full
  meson install -C build-full --no-rebuild --tags runtime

Common dependencies
-------------------

Build tools:
- Meson
- Ninja
- CMake (for bundled idTech2 ericw-tools build)
- gcc/g++
- pkg-config
- git
- wget + unzip (if downloading gamepacks)
- svn (if using `download_gamepacks=yes|all`)

Libraries:
- Qt Core/Gui/Widgets/Svg/Network/Multimedia/OpenGL(+OpenGLWidgets)
- glib-2.0
- libxml2
- libpng
- zlib
- libjpeg
- OpenGL
- assimp (or `-Dassimp_internal=true`)
- oneTBB (for bundled ericw-tools)
- Embree 4.x (for bundled ericw-tools `light`)

Windows (MSYS2)
---------------

Use a MINGW shell (`mingw64` recommended):

  pacman -S --needed base-devel git svn unzip
  pacman -S --needed mingw-w64-x86_64-{toolchain,meson,ninja,cmake,pkgconf,qt6-base,qt6-svg,qt6-multimedia,assimp,libxml2,libpng,glib2,libjpeg-turbo,zlib,tbb,embree}

Then:

  meson setup build-msys2 --prefix "$PWD/install" -Dbuild_profile=release -Dinstall_data=true -Dinstall_dlls=true -Ddownload_gamepacks=allinone
  meson compile -C build-msys2
  meson install -C build-msys2 --no-rebuild --tags runtime
  ./install/radiant.exe

Legacy Makefile entrypoint (still available)
--------------------------------------------

Direct `make` usage remains available for compatibility/manual workflows:

  make -j$(nproc)
  make BUILD=debug -j$(nproc)

Meson is the recommended entrypoint for editor integration and daily builds.

Bundled idTech2 ericw-tools install path
----------------------------------------

`meson install --tags runtime` and `make binaries` now stage bundled ericw tools under:

- `install/ericw/qbsp.[ExecutableType]`
- `install/ericw/light.[ExecutableType]`
- `install/ericw/vis.[ExecutableType]`

This matches the default build-menu paths used by Quake/Quake2-family gamepacks.
